# Agave (Parry's agave, a century plant): a ROSETTE of broad, thick, rigid blue-grey leaves (~1.5-3 m across), the outer
# ones spreading and curving up off the ground, the inner ones upright, each widest near its middle and ending in a
# point. It grows ON ITS OWN in the hot desert (its Placement block: no tree needed); Climate Desert - no tree's - so it
# is never a tree's undergrowth.
# The leaves are the modules: one blade each (`Section`: wide, thin, a gutter on top; `Swell`: widest near the middle;
# `Tip`: a closed point), no leaf cards. The crown starts above the ground on a short hidden trunk: the outer leaves
# rise off it.
